  "title": "Supplementary Table S23. Attrition sensitivity analyses.",
  "panel": "A",
  "panel_title": "Panel a. Baseline (2011) characteristics of participants retained in the analytical cohort versus 2011-only participants.",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Values are mean (SD) or n (%) on an available-data basis (per-variable N: 2,785–3,197 retained; 1,518–1,757 2011-only). Standardised differences are the mean difference divided by the pooled SD (continuous) or the proportion difference divided by sqrt(p(1−p)) (binary). The table describes baseline comparability for the attrition sensitivity analysis; it is not a re-derivation of the primary BAA. BMI summaries exclude values outside the plausible range of 12–60 kg m⁻²."
